Steps to Set Up SAML Federation
1. Configure Ping Identity as IdP
Create a new SAML Application in PingFederate.
Define the SP Metadata provided by your Spring Boot app.
Configure the Assertion Attributes.
Configure the Signing Certificate & Encryption Key.
Configure SAML Bindings (typically, HTTP-Redirect for SSO requests and HTTP-POST for responses).
Enable Single Sign-On (SSO).
Export the IdP Metadata XML.
2. Configure the Spring Boot Application as SP
Use Spring Security SAML to configure the application as an SP.
Import the IdP's Public Key to verify the SAML assertion.
Configure SP Metadata and provide it to the IdP.
Implement SAML Response Processing.
